---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="What I can help with — DuBose, M.D." active="help" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-block:clamp(56px,8vw,88px)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Scope of care</span>
          <h1>What I can help with</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          Most of what makes people feel better isn&rsquo;t exotic.
          It&rsquo;s ordinary medicine — done carefully, with enough time,
          by someone who knows you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · The situations I'm built for -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Where I&rsquo;m most useful</span>
        <h2>The situations I&rsquo;m built for</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards c2">
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;It&rsquo;s several things at once.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Blood pressure, weight, sleep, energy, stress — each one
            manageable, together overwhelming. We&rsquo;ll sort out
            what&rsquo;s urgent, what matters most, and what can wait — then
            work through it in order, at a humane pace.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;Something came back abnormal.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            A lab result, a scan, a number in your portal with no explanation
            attached. I&rsquo;ll go through it with you: what it means, what
            it doesn&rsquo;t, what to do next, and what to watch. Worry
            shrinks when things get explained.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I have conditions that deserve more than 15 minutes.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Diabetes, blood pressure, cholesterol, thyroid — managed, not
            just refilled: medications reviewed, complications watched for,
            numbers trending where we agreed they should go.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;Nothing&rsquo;s wrong — yet.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            You want a doctor who knows your baseline, watches your trends,
            keeps screening on schedule, and tells you the truth about what
            matters. Prevention works best before it&rsquo;s urgent.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card span">
          <h4>&ldquo;Honestly, my health and my life are tangled together.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            The stress is wrecking the sleep, the sleep is wrecking the
            eating, the money worry sits under all of it — and your body is
            keeping score. This is real medicine territory, and it&rsquo;s
            the kind I take most seriously. We look at the whole picture,
            treat what needs treating, and work the rest — one realistic step
            at a time. Where a counselor or financial professional is the
            right tool, I&rsquo;ll help you find a good one and stay involved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · The everyday medicine — open list, no boxes -->
  <section class="section" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Day to day</span>
        <h2>The everyday medicine</h2>
        <p class="lede">Membership covers the full range of adult primary care.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps c3">
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Ongoing conditions</h4>
          <p>High blood pressure, diabetes and prediabetes, cholesterol,
          thyroid, asthma, acid reflux, gout, migraine, and more.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>When you&rsquo;re sick</h4>
          <p>Infections, colds that won&rsquo;t quit, UTIs, rashes, stomach
          trouble, injuries that don&rsquo;t need an ER, &ldquo;is this
          serious?&rdquo;</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Prevention &amp; screening</h4>
          <p>Annual reviews, cancer screening on schedule, vaccines planned,
          risk assessment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Medications</h4>
          <p>Reviewed as a whole: what&rsquo;s working, what&rsquo;s
          redundant, what&rsquo;s interacting; new prescriptions and refills
          handled without games.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Mind &amp; mood</h4>
          <p>Depression and anxiety, adult ADHD, stress, burnout, and sleep
          problems including insomnia — treated seriously within primary
          care, referred wisely when needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Lifestyle &amp; habits</h4>
          <p>Sleep, weight — including modern weight-loss medications where
          appropriate — exercise, nutrition, alcohol and tobacco: as
          medicine, not a lecture.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:40px">
        Plus: labs and imaging ordered and explained, specialist referrals
        with a real handoff, coordination when several doctors are involved —
        and the paperwork of being a patient handled without extra charges:
        disability and FMLA forms, letters, prior authorizations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · What I don't do -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Boundaries</span>
          <h2>What I don&rsquo;t do — and what happens instead</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Emergencies</b>
          <p>Chest pain, stroke signs, severe injury — that&rsquo;s 911 and
          the ER, always. Afterward, I help you make sense of what happened
          and what comes next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Hospital care</b>
          <p>If you&rsquo;re admitted, the hospital&rsquo;s physicians run
          the admission. I stay informed and manage your landing when
          you&rsquo;re home.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialist-led conditions, alone</b>
          <p>Some conditions need an oncologist, cardiologist, or
          rheumatologist leading. I refer well, co-manage, and keep the whole
          picture — I don&rsquo;t pretend to replace them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Mental health beyond primary care&rsquo;s safe reach</b>
          <p>Serious psychiatric illness and addiction medicine beyond my
          scope get honest triage and a warm handoff, not improvisation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Children</b>
          <p>Adults only (18+).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
          If I&rsquo;m ever not the right doctor for something, I&rsquo;ll
          tell you directly — that&rsquo;s part of what you&rsquo;re paying
          for.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Not sure whether your situation fits?</h2>
        <p>
          That&rsquo;s exactly what the free conversation is for. Tell me
          what&rsquo;s going on — I&rsquo;ll tell you honestly whether I can
          help, and point you somewhere good if I can&rsquo;t.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">How the membership works &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
